<rml>
<head>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="theme.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="sidebar_hud.rcss"/>
</head>
<body data-model="sidebar_hud">
    <!-- Tier 7 sidebar HUD (game::draw_panels). A PERSISTENT, render-only, continuous
         every-turn document — NOT a modal open/loop/close screen. Opened once during
         gameplay and synced each turn; modal screens stack above it by open order.

         STRUCTURAL PIVOT (slice 3, 2026-06-20): ONE hand-authored flex column inside a
         single absolutely-positioned container = the sidebar rect (C++ injects
         left/top/width/height each frame so it tracks resize + SIDEBAR_POSITION). This
         REPLACES the slice 1-2d per-panel position:absolute machinery. Curses suppression
         is now WHOLE-SIDEBAR (game::draw_panels early-returns when the HUD is active), so
         the column owns the entire sidebar — every present panel is a row here, either a
         migrated producer's RML or a visible "[name]" placeholder (never a silent blank;
         post-rip-out there is no curses fallback).

         The column is data-driven: C++ walks the current layout in order and fills `rows`
         (one {rml, flex} per present panel). Flex-height sentinels (-1 minimap / -2 log)
         get row.flex=true → flex-grow:1 so they absorb the remaining height. -->
    <!-- Qud screen chrome (Phase 2): top status strip (2 rows: name/needs/date, then
         HP/stamina/mana bars) + bottom effects/hostiles strip (1 row). Carved out of
         the terrain viewport by sidebar_hud_top_rows()/_bottom_rows(); rects placed by
         sidebar_hud_apply_rect() each sync alongside #hud-sidebar. -->
    <div id="hud-topbar">
        <div class="hud-strip-row" data-rml="topbar_rml"></div>
        <div class="hud-strip-row" data-rml="topbar2_rml"></div>
    </div>
    <div id="hud-botbar">
        <div class="hud-strip-row" data-rml="botbar_rml"></div>
    </div>
    <div id="hud-sidebar" class="hud-sidebar">
        <div class="hud-row" data-for="row : rows" data-class-flex="row.flex">
            <div class="hud-row-header" data-if="row.title != ''" data-rml="row.title"></div>
            <div class="hud-row-body" data-rml="row.rml"></div>
        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
